crossing-horn is a small command-line tool for the arithmetic around a
locomotive train horn at a public grade crossing in the United States.

  crossing-horn onset <mph>
    When the horn has to start under 49 CFR 222.21(b): 15 to 20 seconds
    before the crossing, capped at one quarter mile above 60 mph.
  crossing-horn intervals <id|"- - o -"> [--csv]
    Expands GCOR 5.8.2 whistle patterns into on/off millisecond
    intervals.
  crossing-horn level <dBA-at-100ft> <distance-ft>
    Free-field inverse-square estimate of a horn's dB(A) at a distance,
    checked against the 96-110 dB(A) band of 49 CFR 229.129.
  crossing-horn list
    Prints the bundled GCOR 5.8.2 signals.

Only the executable is installed. Source code and the OCaml library
are at https://github.com/bosshorncom-cmd/crossing-horn
